  "_comment": "The partitioned 30 Hz chain with yolo taking the WHOLE P cluster per frame, and nav and control free to use any hart of the E cluster rather than one named hart each. Width is left at 1 for both: gen_mb_shard profiles fused_full and mlp_control at topo_0 only, so a wider nav would have no measured cost behind it. This asks only WHERE they run, not how wide, so every cost is still measured. yolo keeps allowed_machines CPU_P + machine_width 4, which is what makes the whole of it IME-eligible (smt.vmadot is legal only on cluster 0, ModelBlaster/artifacts/ime_isa_probe/FINDINGS.md).",
